{
  "rationale": "This is iteration 0, so there is no race telemetry or integration feedback yet. The geometry is a conservative baseline built from the contract. Five sensors at 10 mm pitch (x = -0.02 to +0.02 m) span 40 mm, more than the 25 mm tape, so the line stays under at least one sensor across the normal lateral error range, and the signal stays linear near the centre. Sensors sit 0.04 m ahead of the axle so they read the line before the wheels reach it, which gives the controller lead time on bends. A 12 mm footprint is used: it gives partial coverage on each sensor for a smooth reading gradient without blurring the edges. Wheel track 0.12 m and radius 0.03 m give a moderate turn authority and a speed capacity suited to the 1.5 m/s average needed. Body width 0.12 m gives an off-track limit of 0.06 m (the floor), and mass 0.8 kg keeps inertia moderate. Expected result: a completed run on the development tracks, with the main limit set by the Integrator's gains rather than by geometry. Hypotheses to test: (1) a 5-sensor, 10 mm pitch array keeps rms_error low on the tighter s-bend and slalom; (2) the 0.04 m lead gives enough margin to hold speed on bends; (3) a wider sensor span would reduce line loss on the slalom.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": -0.01, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.01, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.04}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "intent": "Baseline geometry: a symmetric 5-sensor line array at 10 mm pitch, 40 mm total span, mounted 0.04 m ahead of the axle, with 12 mm footprints. Chosen to give a linear steering signal across the tape, a lead on bends, and a body that stays within the off-track limit. This establishes a reference point for later geometry changes; no change is claimed yet, and the expected result is a completed run on the development tracks with line loss limited to bend entries.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation"
    ]
  },
  "learning": "No evidence yet. Next iteration should check whether the sensor pitch and lead give the Integrator a usable signal on all three development tracks, and whether line loss or off-track events appear on the slalom, which would point to span or lead changes."
}
